WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:06.335
In under two minutes, you will add a lighting company to your contest, and see how families ask for a quote.

00:00:06.335 --> 00:00:07.424
We start on the map.

00:00:08.328 --> 00:00:11.660
Open your web browser, and go to SoCal Lights dot app.

00:00:13.454 --> 00:00:15.876
This is the SoCal Lights home page.

00:00:15.876 --> 00:00:18.366
A message asks to use your location.

00:00:18.366 --> 00:00:19.712
Tap Use my location.

00:00:21.453 --> 00:00:23.669
Your browser asks for permission.

00:00:23.669 --> 00:00:24.321
Tap Allow.

00:00:27.860 --> 00:00:30.356
Look at the top right corner of the map.

00:00:30.356 --> 00:00:31.573
See the three dots?

00:00:31.573 --> 00:00:32.121
Tap them.

00:00:33.726 --> 00:00:35.688
In the menu, tap Contests.

00:00:37.380 --> 00:00:38.009
Tap Mine.

00:00:38.009 --> 00:00:39.957
These are the contests you run.

00:00:41.634 --> 00:00:43.656
Tap Manage, next to your contest.

00:00:43.656 --> 00:00:45.024
This is your dashboard.

00:00:46.905 --> 00:00:49.912
Tap Details, and scroll to Presenting installer.

00:00:52.146 --> 00:00:56.267
Type the company's name, the email for quote requests, and their website.

00:01:01.410 --> 00:01:02.578
Tap Save changes.

00:01:02.578 --> 00:01:05.950
This adds a Get a quote button to your contest page.

00:01:08.258 --> 00:01:12.112
Now a neighbor opens the contest page, and taps Get a quote.

00:01:14.310 --> 00:01:17.233
They add their name, and what they would like done.

00:01:17.233 --> 00:01:19.875
They must tick the box to share their details.

00:01:19.875 --> 00:01:21.392
Then they tap Send request.

00:01:25.147 --> 00:01:28.769
Next up: Installer profiles and Installed by.
